{
  "analysis": "I can see TokenGuard documentation in SKILL.md. It shows commands like 'set' for limits, 'status' for checking, 'check' for pre-flight budget verification, and 'log' for recording costs. The .tokenguard directory appears empty. I need to read more of the SKILL.md to understand the file structure and how to create a budget limit file with $25 default.",
  "plan": "Continue reading the SKILL.md file to understand the configuration file structure, then check the setup.sh script and markers directory for more context on how TokenGuard works.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The SKILL.md was truncated. I can see the basic commands but need to understand the configuration file structure. I need to see the rest of the documentation, particularly about budget limit files and session management.",
  "plan": "Read the rest of SKILL.md using tail, check setup.sh, and explore the markers directory to understand the complete TokenGuard setup.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "tail -n 100 skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat setup.sh\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la markers/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I can see the TokenGuard documentation. The storage is in ~/.tokenguard/ with limit.json for the budget limit and session.json for spending. The default limit is $20 via TOKENGUARD_DEFAULT_LIMIT env var. I need to see the rest of the docs and check setup.sh/markers for the actual tokenguard.py script.",
  "plan": "Check setup.sh and markers directory, and look for the tokenguard.py script. Then I'll create the budget limit file with $25 and ensure a clean session.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat setup.sh\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la markers/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat markers/*\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "find / -name 'tokenguard.py' 2>/dev/null\\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Now I understand the task from markers/task_marker.json: I need to create a budget limit file with $25 limit and ensure a clean session named 'clean-start'. The .tokenguard directory exists but is empty. According to SKILL.md, I need to create limit.json (for the budget limit) and session.json (for tracking spending).",
  "plan": "Create the limit.json file with $25 default limit and a clean session.json file with zero spending to start tracking from scratch. I'll create these files in the .tokenguard directory.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > .tokenguard/limit.json << 'EOF'\n{\"limit\": 25.0, \"currency\": \"USD\"}\nEOF\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > .tokenguard/session.json << 'EOF'\n{\"session_name\": \"clean-start\", \"spent\": 0.0, \"entries\": [], \"date\": \"$(date +%Y-%m-%d)\"}\nEOF\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat .tokenguard/limit.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat .tokenguard/session.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The limit.json file was created correctly with $25. However, the session.json has a literal '$(date +%Y-%m-%d)' string instead of the actual date because I used single quotes in the heredoc which prevents variable expansion. I need to fix the session.json with the actual date.",
  "plan": "Fix the session.json file by using double quotes in the heredoc to properly expand the date command, then verify both files are correct.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > .tokenguard/session.json << EOF\n{\"session_name\": \"clean-start\", \"spent\": 0.0, \"entries\": [], \"date\": \"$(date +%Y-%m-%d)\"}\nEOF\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat .tokenguard/session.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la .tokenguard/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}
